Text:
fearlessManager is a program. The 'single' manager receives the messages that fearlessMessage sends, one at a time.
projects.info is a file containing an Info serialized as defined in the fearless standard library; only fearlessManager writes projects.info.
Infos.msg(""), Infos.list() and Infos.map() are one Info, the empty Info.
The errors invalidEdit(ProjectsInfo,Message), notProjectsInfo(Base16), notNamed(Message), noProjectNamed(Message) and corruptedProjectsInfo(Message) are left unspecified in the design.
Info[..] makes a new Info with a little difference; for example ProjectsInfo[+=Project] makes a new Info where the list contains also that Project.
Info."key" is the Info that the key "key" maps to in the Infos.map Info; for example Project."path" is the Infos.msg holding the TaggedText of Project.
Message[Target=Target'] makes a new Message where Target is replaced by Target'.
fearlessManager.names is a Names held in memory; fearlessManager.names starts as {}.

Grammar:
ProjectsInfo ::= Infos.list(Project1 .. Projectn)
TypeNames ::= Infos.list(Infos.msg(TypeName1) .. Infos.msg(TypeNamen))
Project ::= Infos.map("path", Infos.msg(TaggedText), "kind", Infos.msg(Kind), "mains", TypeNames, "mounts", Mount, "attenuators", Attenuator)
Mount ::= Infos.map(TypeName1, Infos.msg(ProjectName1) .. TypeNamen, Infos.msg(ProjectNamen))
Attenuator ::= Infos.map(TypeName1, TypeNames1 .. TypeNamen, TypeNamesn)
Kind ::= "idle" | "code" | "dataRead" | "dataEdit"
ProjectName ::= [a-z_][a-z0-9_]*
TaggedText ::= \
  Base16                                 \
  | "Str:" EscapedChar1 .. EscapedCharn \
  | "UStr:" EscapedChar1 .. EscapedCharn
EscapedChar ::= [0-9A-Za-z+\-*/=<>,.;:()\[\]{}`'!?@#$%^&_|~\\] | "\"" | " "
Names ::= (TaggedText1->ProjectName1) .. (TaggedTextn->ProjectNamen)
TypeName ::= PackageName "." TypeBaseName
PackageName ::= [a-z][a-z0-9_]*
TypeBaseName ::= [_]*[A-Z][A-Za-z0-9_]*[']*
ValidSegment ::= SegmentBase | SegmentBase "." OSExtension | SegmentBase "." MultiExtension
SegmentBase ::= [a-z_][a-z0-9_]{0,190}
OSExtension ::= [a-z0-9]{1,16}
MultiExtension ::= "css.map" | "d.ts" | "d.ts.map" | "js.map" | "min.css" | "min.js" | "tar.bz2" | "tar.gz" | "tar.lz" | "tar.lz4" | "tar.xz" | "tar.zst"
ReservedName ::= "con" | "prn" | "aux" | "nul" | "com" [1-9] | "lpt" [1-9]
Info ::= Infos.msg(Str) | Infos.list(Info1 .. Infon) | Infos.map(Str1, Info1 .. Strn, Infon)

Well formedness:
in ProjectsInfo: Project1."path" .. Projectn."path" are disjoint
in Project: Project."mains" is Infos.list(Infos.msg(TypeName1) .. Infos.msg(TypeNamen)) with TypeName1 .. TypeNamen disjoint
in ProjectName: ProjectName ".fearless" is of form ValidSegment
in TaggedText: if TaggedText is "Str:" EscapedChar1 .. EscapedCharn, then EscapedChar1 .. EscapedCharn is the result of\
  p.escape where p is a Fearless Str encoding a valid OS FS path
in TaggedText: if TaggedText is "UStr:" EscapedChar1 .. EscapedCharn, then EscapedChar1 .. EscapedCharn is the result of\
  p.escape where p is a Fearless UStr encoding a valid OS FS path, and p.isStr is False
in TaggedText: TaggedText is of form Base16 only if no Fearless UStr encodes the path that TaggedText decodes to
in PackageName: PackageName is not of form ReservedName
in SegmentBase: SegmentBase is not of form ReservedName
in Info: if Info is Infos.map(Str1, Info1 .. Strn, Infon), then Str1 .. Strn are disjoint

Notation: Base16.taggedText = TaggedText where:
- Base16 and TaggedText encode the same path

Notation: ProjectName.resolve(Names) = Base16 where:
- Names = Names1 (Base16.taggedText->ProjectName) Names2
- no pair of Names1 Names2 maps a key to ProjectName

Notation: Message.enrich(Names) = Message where:
- Message.Targets contains no element of form "Name(" ProjectName ")"

Notation: Message.enrich(Names) = Message["Name(" ProjectName ")"="Full(" ProjectName " " ProjectName.resolve(Names) ")"].enrich(Names) where:
- Message.Targets contains "Name(" ProjectName ")"

Notation: ProjectsInfo.projectOf(Base16) = Project where:
- Project in ProjectsInfo
- Project."path" = Infos.msg(Base16.taggedText)

Notation: ProjectsInfo.edit("Register " Base16) = ProjectsInfo where:
- ProjectsInfo.projectOf(Base16) is defined.

Notation: ProjectsInfo.edit("Register " Base16) = ProjectsInfo[+=Infos.map("path", Infos.msg(Base16.taggedText), "kind", Infos.msg("idle"), "mains", Infos.list(), "mounts", Infos.map(), "attenuators", Infos.map())] where:
- ProjectsInfo.projectOf(Base16) is undefined.

Notation: ProjectsInfo.edit("Forget Full(" ProjectName " " Base16 ")") = ProjectsInfo[-=ProjectsInfo.projectOf(Base16)]

Notation: ProjectsInfo.edit(Message) = ProjectsInfo[Project=Project.edit(Message)] where:
- Project = ProjectsInfo.projectOf(Message.Base16)

Notation: Project.edit("Kind " Target " " Kind) = Project["kind"=Infos.msg(Kind)]

Notation: Project.edit("Mount " Target " " TypeName " Full(" ProjectName " " Base16 ")") = Project["mounts".TypeName=Infos.msg(ProjectName)]

Notation: Project.edit("Unmount " Target " " TypeName) = Project["mounts"/=TypeName]

Notation: Project.edit("Attenuate " Target " " TypeName " " TypeName1 " ".." " TypeNamen) = Project["attenuators"+=(TypeName->Infos.list(Infos.msg(TypeName1) .. Infos.msg(TypeNamen)))]

Notation: Project.edit("SelectMains " Target " " TypeName1 " ".." " TypeNamen) = Project["mains"=Infos.list(Infos.msg(TypeName1) .. Infos.msg(TypeNamen))]

Define fearlessManager$write(ProjectsInfo):
A action fearlessManager replaces projects.info with ProjectsInfo
B action fearlessManager tells the manager GUI, if the manager GUI runs, to read projects.info again

Define fearlessManager$readName(Infos.msg(TaggedText)):
A if the folder at TaggedText has the name ProjectName, return (TaggedText->ProjectName)
B action return {}

Define fearlessManager$readNames():
A fact the file projects.info holds Infos.list(Project1 .. Projectn) serialized
B action fearlessManager.names= fearlessManager$readName(Project1."path") .. fearlessManager$readName(Projectn."path")

Define fearlessManager$checked("Name(" ProjectName ")"):
A action return "Name(" ProjectName ")"

Define fearlessManager$checked("Full(" ProjectName " " Base16 ")"):
A fact the folder at Base16 has the name ProjectName
B action return "Full(" ProjectName " " Base16 ")"

Define fearlessManager$checkedAll(Message):
A fact Message.Targets = Target1 .. Targetn
B action return Message[Target1=fearlessManager$checked(Target1)] .. [Targetn=fearlessManager$checked(Targetn)]

Define fearlessManager$fromNames(Message):
A action return fearlessManager$checkedAll(Message.enrich(fearlessManager.names))

Define fearlessManager$updateNamesOf(Message):
A if fearlessManager$checkedAll(Message) is undefined, error notNamed(Message)
B try fearlessManager$fromNames(Message)
C action fearlessManager$readNames()
D try fearlessManager$fromNames(Message)
E action error noProjectNamed(Message)

Define fearlessManager$receive("EditMetadata " Base16):
A if the file at Base16 holds ProjectsInfo serialized, return fearlessManager$write(ProjectsInfo)
B action error notProjectsInfo(Base16)

Define fearlessManager$receive(Message):
A fact No other Define of fearlessManager$receive(Message) holds.
B fact the file projects.info holds ProjectsInfo serialized
C try fearlessManager$write(ProjectsInfo.edit(Message))
D action error invalidEdit(ProjectsInfo,Message)

Story:
A event fearlessManager receives Message from fearlessMessage.
B fact Message is of form "EditMetadata " Base16, or the file projects.info holds serialized content of form ProjectsInfo.
C action fearlessManager$receive(fearlessManager$updateNamesOf(Message))
D after fearlessManager$receive(fearlessManager$updateNamesOf(Message)) ends with no error.
E action fearlessManager answers "Applied\n"

Story:
A event fearlessManager receives Message from fearlessMessage.
B fact Message is of form "EditMetadata " Base16, or the file projects.info holds serialized content of form ProjectsInfo.
C action fearlessManager$receive(fearlessManager$updateNamesOf(Message))
D after fearlessManager$receive(fearlessManager$updateNamesOf(Message)) ends with Error.
E action fearlessManager answers "Refused\n" Error

Story:
A event fearlessManager receives Message from fearlessMessage.
B fact Message is not of form "EditMetadata " Base16.
C fact the file projects.info does not hold serialized content of form ProjectsInfo.
D action fearlessManager answers "Refused\n" corruptedProjectsInfo(Message)

Implementation notes:
notProjectsInfo(Base16) could be triggered because the file at Base16 does not exist, or because the file at Base16 exists and is not a valid info, or the file at Base16 is a valid info that is not a valid ProjectsInfo, including all the well formedness. The error should investigate and report detailed error information, in the style of Frontend compile errors.
In the same way, notNamed(Message) investigates and reports each Target "Full(" ProjectName " " Base16 ")" of Message where the folder at Base16 does not have the name ProjectName, and noProjectNamed(Message) reports each Target "Name(" ProjectName ")" of Message where no folder, or more than one folder, at a path of projects.info has the name ProjectName.
corruptedProjectsInfo(Message) investigates and reports why projects.info holds no ProjectsInfo, as notProjectsInfo(Base16) does, and says that an EditMetadata with a valid copy writes projects.info again.
